verification/ISOLATION_SOURCE_AUDIT.md:98:The pinned release contains the credential vault; these findings do not rely on vault code from a newer commit. Vault entries and external-vault unlock tokens are scoped to the Hermes home, not separately to each Slack sender. A browser task ID does not add an owner field to a vault entry. Origin checks prevent filling credentials on the wrong website; they do not decide which human may use a saved login for the correct website.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:10:2. The backend checks private-DM membership, resolves that handle in that profile's encrypted vault and checks the provider-reported HTTPS page against the saved exact origin.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:12:4. Provider output is scrubbed against saved secrets and encrypted prior redaction values before returning to Clanker. State and operator keys are in the protected gateway home.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:14:The consumer project's existing log setting is `show_all`; it was not changed. Composio may retain tool arguments, including the selected credential. This handoff is not a claim that provider logging, its internal agent or browser content cannot access secrets. Current host-generated-code permissions also do not independently establish a secrets boundary.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:20:The initial backend assigned sessions to conversation/profile contexts; it never accepted provider IDs from the model. The 2026-10-06 invitation patch additionally binds new state to workspace, authenticated requester and home, and refuses recorded provider-session ownership collisions. It does not adopt legacy state automatically. A consistent short session name reuses that requester's cookies between completed tasks. Before reuse, the backend checks whether the browser has stopped; an expired browser starts fresh without automatically resending credentials. STOP_TASK stops a task; it does not establish that cookies or the remote browser profile were deleted. Stop now reports profile_retained=null (unknown). Revocation that requires a verified purge remains blocked and reports cleanup pending for this provider. Vault logins remain saved. A missing dispatch acknowledgement blocks automatic retry until an operator reconciles it. A confirmed upstream HTTP 422 body-validation rejection clears that attempt flag, preserves the previous task/session, and returns HTTP 422 without replaying it. The exact upstream HTTP 400 stopped-browser rejection also releases the failed attempt and discards its expired browser IDs; other HTTP 400 responses remain unknown.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:26:- 48 focused tests passed after the rejection, browser-expiry and verification-code fixes: Browser Tool and Browser Use adapters, encrypted vault behavior, ownership checks and Slack membership.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:29:- A live public demo login passed through the encrypted native vault and Browser Tool, including credential fill and a separate login submission. The demo browser was stopped afterward.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:45:The adapter now sends only the password under the hostname key and supplies the account identifier separately. It encrypts the full supplied secret for output redaction, including passwords containing colons. The field-substitution regression and the existing ownership, vault, lifecycle and membership checks passed: 51 focused tests. Gateway PID 56183 is running the fix. The replacement vault callback and yyovil Slack OIDC are verified. A new Slack test pauses after filling for inspection before Google submission.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:49:Live Google verification-code handoff is now exercised: the owner submitted the SMS code in the private vault form, the task resumed automatically, the single-use encrypted payload was consumed, and Browser Tool filled and submitted it. Google advanced to a Redmi 10 Power notification challenge (number 60). Full sign-in remains pending that owner action; no code or password value is stored in repository evidence.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:53:After owner device approval, Clanker’s account inspection and the provider screenshot both confirmed the signed-in Google Account email itsyyovil@gmail.com. The exercised flow passed: Slack private request, encrypted vault password, Browser Tool password fill, private SMS-code form, automatic resume, code submission, device approval, and final account verification. The 51 focused checks also passed. No Gmail, ChatGPT signup, recovery, reset, purchase, commit, or publication action was performed.
docs/decisions/2026-10-05-composio-browser-vault.md:55:Clanker called STOP_TASK after verification. The prior claim that this removed cookies (profile_retained=false) was not supported by a cookie-deletion receipt and has been corrected. The encrypted vault password remains available. The earlier pending callback, SMS, and device-challenge notes above describe resolved test phases. Runtime result_verified remains false for provider reports alone; this acceptance additionally uses operator screenshot review and the owner’s confirmation. It does not establish cross-requester account authorization. See the [invitation and isolation limits](2026-10-06-vault-invitations.md).
